title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Decision branches
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: A Decision step has one exit per branch plus 'Otherwise'. The first branch whose condition holds is followed. Adding, renaming, reordering or removing a branch changes the exits on the step at once, and a removed branch takes its line with it.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Select a Decision step\nor add one from 'Conditions' in the list"
screen br "'Branches'\n'Branches are checked from the top. The first one that holds is followed; if none do, the case follows Otherwise.'\nEach branch: its name, up and down arrows, a bin, and a condition builder\nFixed row: 'Otherwise: when no branch above holds.'"
click c1 "Click 'Add a branch'"
process p1 "'Branch 2' appears with one starting condition\nThe step gets another exit on the canvas, labelled with the branch name"
input i1 "Rename the branch"
process p2 "The exit's label and the label on its line change with the name"
click c2 "Click the up or down arrow on a branch"
process p3 "The order changes, and the order is the order they are checked"
click c3 "Click the bin on a branch"
decision d1 "Did the branch have a line to another step?"
process p4 "The line is removed with the branch\nThe other branches and Otherwise keep theirs"
process p5 "The branch is simply removed"
screen w1 "A branch with no line shows\n'This branch does not lead anywhere yet. Connect it below, under Next steps.'\nOtherwise with no line shows 'It does not lead anywhere yet.'"
click c4 "Under 'Next steps', pick where each branch leads"
process p6 "Lines are drawn; the labels on them are the branch names"
decision d2 "Does every exit lead somewhere?"
process p7 "The checks stay quiet"
process p8 "Checks list 'Needs fixing' for the exit, with 'Go to node'\nPublishing is blocked until it is connected"
end e1 "The Decision routes every case somewhere"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Check a workflow before publishing"

s1 --> br
br --> c1 --> p1 --> i1 --> p2
br --> c2 --> p3
br --> c3 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p4 --> w1
d1 -->|No| p5 --> w1
p2 --> w1
p3 --> w1
w1 --> c4 --> p6 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| p7 --> e1
d2 -->|No| p8 --> g1
